{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"pennywise-ash-comet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nClosing an epic under `verify.require_plan_review_for_close = true` requires a plan-review attestation that passes `PlanValidityProfile.CLOSE`. CLOSE deliberately tolerates code drift (`docs/plan-review-gate.md`, 'Close-time attestation gate': it 'does not reject ordinary implementation HEAD or reviewed-file drift'), but it still blocks on **own-material drift** and, when `enforce_plan_material_pins = true`, on pin health.\n\nFor an epic those two conditions are met almost by construction, because executing the epic is what changes them:\n\n- An epic's description is routinely re-scoped mid-flight as its census is corrected, and its child set grows as slices are decomposed. Both are own-material edits.\n- Each child that closes moves its own material, so the epic's pins go `stale-pin-drift`.\n\nObserved on 2026-10-31 closing epic `e12f-a994-29d3-4f72` (unhygienic-houndlike-arrowworm) with all 9 children closed and all 6 acceptance criteria independently re-verified green on the landed tree:\n\n```\nplan-review close gate: stale-material: the plan was materially edited since review --\nchanged: description (3539 -> 5626 chars), children (5 -> 9 children) ...\nHealth: stale-pin-drift (enforced); phase planning -> execution (compatible);\ntargets: 596b-919d child stale-pin-drift, b939-bc68 child stale-pin-drift,\ncb2b-7446 child stale-pin-drift, e123-cf0f child stale-pin-drift,\ned5a-3042 child stale-pin-drift\n```\n\nThe gate explicitly exonerates checkbox ticking ('box state is normalized out of the fingerprint'), so this is not an artifact of marking the ACs done.\n\nThe two available exits are both poor:\n\n1. Re-run `review-plan` on the epic. This costs 15-20 minutes and a full LLM pass to review a plan whose work is 100 percent delivered and verified. The **completion floor** (ADR 0024) exists to stop exactly this re-litigation of settled acceptance text, but it is evidence-gated behind `verify.completion_floor_active`, which defaults `false` and is not set in the committed `rebar.toml` -- so today the re-review is a byte-identical full review.\n2. The human-only `--force=<reason>` break-glass. Agents are forbidden from using it, so every epic close becomes an operator interrupt, and the forced close records no certification -- the audit signal is lost precisely on the tickets whose work was most thoroughly verified.\n\nThe cost is structural, not incidental: it is paid once per epic, at the moment the epic has the most completed evidence behind it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 An epic whose children are all `closed` with valid completion-verifier attestations, and whose own acceptance criteria are satisfied, has a documented close path that requires neither a fresh full LLM plan review nor `--force`. The path must be reachable by an agent.\n- [ ] AC2 The chosen path preserves the audit property that motivated the gate: a close taken through it records a certification, so 'closed without a signature' remains the durable signal that validation did not pass. Checked by asserting a signature is present after a close taken through the new path.\n- [ ] AC3 The path does not weaken the gate for the cases it was built for. An epic with an unclosed child, a force-closed child, or unmet own acceptance criteria still blocks. Checked by one test per case.\n- [ ] AC4 `docs/plan-review-gate.md` documents when own-material drift and pin drift block an epic close and which path applies, so the next operator does not rediscover this at close time.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nChanging `verify.completion_floor_active`'s default. That flag gates finding-suppression inside a review that still runs; this bug is about not needing the review at all. The two interact and the floor may well be part of the answer, but flipping a calibration-gated default is its own decision with its own evidence bar.","id":"0ed3-b6e3-994e-4b99","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Epic close has no proportionate path once every child has closed: own-material drift blocks, and re-review re-litigates settled work"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793467013786565001,"uuid":"1869bbe2-695a-4227-9b95-8e208191eaec"}